# Windows portability build + test guard.
#
# DISABLED (see .github/workflows/DISABLED_WORKFLOWS_POLICY.md): GitHub Actions
# billing is operator-blocked for v1.0, so this ships as `.yml.disabled` and
# does NOT run. It exists so Windows portability — the surface the Windows
# worker fleet (docs/build-plan/BUILD_STATUS_WINDOWS.md) is hardening — is
# guarded the moment CI billing is restored: rename the suffix to `.yml` and it
# runs. NO THEATER: this file has never executed in CI (zero runner minutes);
# the fleet's Windows verification today is the per-brief real-Windows
# `cargo build`/`cargo test` runs recorded in each PR.
#
# Mirrors the cross-platform `test` matrix job in `ci.yml.disabled`, narrowed to
# windows-latest with an explicit `cargo build --workspace` first so a Windows
# *link* regression (e.g. a non-portable native dependency like the kryptering
# PKCS#11 break the fleet cfg-gated off Windows in #2905) fails loudly and early,
# before the test compile.
name: Windows build

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
  workflow_dispatch:

jobs:
  windows-build:
    runs-on: windows-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable
      - uses: Swatinem/rust-cache@v2
      - name: Build workspace (Windows link guard)
        run: cargo build --workspace
      - name: Test workspace (Windows)
        # --no-fail-fast so a single Windows-only failure does not mask the
        # rest of the inventory when this guard is first re-enabled.
        run: cargo test --workspace --no-fail-fast
